WEBVTT

00:00:45.547 --> 00:00:47.673
- Aw. He's using his jacket

00:00:47.674 --> 00:00:49.717
as some kind of
security blanket.

00:00:49.768 --> 00:00:51.602
- That's so cute and pathetic.

00:00:51.603 --> 00:00:54.897
- It really is.
You do you, weirdo!

00:00:54.898 --> 00:00:57.441
- Oh, hey, guys. I'm just
sucking on my jacket.

00:00:57.442 --> 00:00:59.818
A Clump-O-Honey candy
got stuck right there

00:00:59.819 --> 00:01:02.571
over a thousand years ago,
and I can still taste it.

00:01:02.572 --> 00:01:04.990
- You know who I bet
would like some of that?

00:01:04.991 --> 00:01:06.325
Me! Zoidberg.

00:01:08.203 --> 00:01:10.412
Oh, no!

00:01:10.413 --> 00:01:12.498
Zoidberg, you residue hog!

00:01:12.499 --> 00:01:14.708
Now all I taste is crab juice.

00:01:14.709 --> 00:01:16.919
- So, buy another jacket candy.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:18.963
- I can't. They
stopped making it

00:01:18.964 --> 00:01:22.091
after it got reclassified
as industrial glue.

00:01:22.092 --> 00:01:25.469
- Ah. Then I, Bender,
will recreate the recipe.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:28.473
Don't forget, I came in
third on MasterChef Junior.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:34.561
- May I have a taste?

00:01:34.562 --> 00:01:37.356
- Sure. You seem like the
kind of guy who has a mouth.

00:01:38.692 --> 00:01:41.860
- Whoa! Diabetic coma!

00:01:41.861 --> 00:01:44.781
- Hm. I better add some
sugar to make it less sweet.

00:01:46.574 --> 00:01:49.118
- And just a touch of treacle

00:01:49.119 --> 00:01:52.246
to remind me of my dear
departed Aunt Juanita.

00:01:52.247 --> 00:01:54.790
She
drowned in treacle.

00:01:54.791 --> 00:01:57.793
- You know I'm
dying on the floor.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.676
So, what do you think?

00:02:05.677 --> 00:02:09.013
- Mm! It's perfect, Bender.
Totally jacket worthy.

00:02:09.014 --> 00:02:11.181
It's a little sticky.

00:02:11.182 --> 00:02:12.975
It's
a lot sticky!

00:02:14.644 --> 00:02:17.521
And there's
something hard in it.

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:23.736
- Luckily, I'm an expert
at fixing human beak bones.

00:02:23.737 --> 00:02:26.488
Are you free Friday for
an expensive appointment?

00:02:26.489 --> 00:02:28.992
- Let me check. Open calendar!

00:02:30.619 --> 00:02:32.786
Shmeird. There's
some old alert

00:02:32.787 --> 00:02:35.039
I set up 20 years ago.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.208
Our babies?!

00:02:38.835 --> 00:02:40.294
- It's time, my love.

00:02:40.295 --> 00:02:42.087
- Oh, Kif!

00:02:42.088 --> 00:02:43.756
- The hell are
you talking about?

00:02:43.757 --> 00:02:46.091
Something to do with
the meatbag life cycle?

00:02:46.092 --> 00:02:48.177
- That's right,
Bender. Many years ago,

00:02:48.178 --> 00:02:50.596
I gave birth to a
clutch of tadpoles

00:02:50.597 --> 00:02:52.389
with Amy by my side.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:54.850
- I have video of the
birth. Wanna see it?

00:02:54.851 --> 00:02:56.018
No!

00:02:56.019 --> 00:02:58.438
- That is the wrong
kind of delivery!

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.192
Oh, Nelly! Oh!

00:03:07.697 --> 00:03:09.573
- Life is disgusting.

00:03:09.574 --> 00:03:11.575
- No, it was beautiful.

00:03:11.576 --> 00:03:14.078
But I was so not
prepared to be a mother.

00:03:14.079 --> 00:03:16.080
- In 20 years,
they'll sprout legs

00:03:16.081 --> 00:03:18.959
and crawl back onto
land as children.

00:03:19.668 --> 00:03:21.628
- I'll be ready then.

00:03:22.796 --> 00:03:25.297
- Well, Amy, are you ready now?

00:03:25.298 --> 00:03:27.174
- Having a family with you

00:03:27.175 --> 00:03:30.552
is the only thing I
want in the whole world.

00:03:30.553 --> 00:03:32.888
- Then can I have your car?
- No!

00:03:32.889 --> 00:03:34.640
- Too late. I
already crashed it.

00:03:41.815 --> 00:03:43.190
- Oh, this is so exciting!

00:03:43.191 --> 00:03:45.651
The birth ceremony
will begin any minute.

00:03:45.652 --> 00:03:47.612
- Thanks for the warning.

00:03:48.571 --> 00:03:50.739
And don't describe it
to me!

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:53.158
- We're here!
- Mom! Dad!

00:03:53.159 --> 00:03:55.369
Oh, I'm so glad you made it!

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:58.205
- Oh, we wouldn't miss the
birth of our grandbabies

00:03:58.206 --> 00:03:59.832
for a million dollars.

00:03:59.833 --> 00:04:02.001
- 'Cause we're so rich,
that's like a penny.

00:04:05.005 --> 00:04:07.631
- Oh, my. It's
the Grand Midwife.

00:04:07.632 --> 00:04:10.175
- I am the Grand Midwife!

00:04:10.176 --> 00:04:11.844
- Big fan!

00:04:11.845 --> 00:04:14.138
- I am Kif of the clan Kroker.

00:04:14.139 --> 00:04:16.473
- I know. I recognize your head.

00:04:16.474 --> 00:04:18.559
- And this is my smizmar, Amy.

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:21.020
We have come to
receive our offspring.

00:04:21.021 --> 00:04:23.314
- As you transition
to parenthood,

00:04:23.315 --> 00:04:25.941
I shall be your
counsel and guide.

00:04:25.942 --> 00:04:29.278
I do so out of solemn
respect for our traditions

00:04:29.279 --> 00:04:31.822
and not for any
optional cash donation

00:04:31.823 --> 00:04:33.907
people sometimes
place in that basket.

00:04:33.908 --> 00:04:35.284
- Thank you.
- It's green,

00:04:35.285 --> 00:04:37.537
and there's a little sign on it.
- Found it!

00:04:39.706 --> 00:04:42.958
- Then the Emergence
shall now commence!

00:04:47.172 --> 00:04:49.757
Or not. It's unpredictable.

00:04:49.758 --> 00:04:52.801
Guess I'll have to wing it.
Anybody here from out of town?

00:04:52.802 --> 00:04:54.762
O-oh!
Here they come.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:06.273
- Oh my. I'm so anxious, my
camouflage reflex is kicking in.

00:05:06.274 --> 00:05:07.775
- No, it's helpful.

00:05:07.776 --> 00:05:10.277
I wanna look cute for
our hundreds of kids.

00:05:11.863 --> 00:05:15.240
- We shall now stand
by, without interfering,

00:05:15.241 --> 00:05:18.369
as we observe the sacred
process known as...

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:19.787
the Winnowing.

00:05:19.788 --> 00:05:21.205
- What's that mean?

00:05:21.206 --> 00:05:23.290
- It means don't
start naming them yet.

00:05:40.267 --> 00:05:41.767
- Four of them made it!

00:05:43.186 --> 00:05:44.812
Well, three and a half.

00:05:44.813 --> 00:05:47.356
- Young creatures
of the Black Lagoon,

00:05:47.357 --> 00:05:49.358
go now to your parents.

00:05:52.904 --> 00:05:54.738
- Uh, can I help you?

00:05:54.739 --> 00:05:55.991
- Over here!

00:05:59.327 --> 00:06:02.329
They're perfect.

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:04.456
- Ew. She's touching them.

00:06:04.457 --> 00:06:07.459
- Cherish these
children, Kif and Amy,

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:09.629
for they are beautiful.

00:06:11.673 --> 00:06:12.673
Eh...

00:06:12.674 --> 00:06:15.634
- Well, in-in the sense that
all children are beautiful.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.396
The transformation is complete!

00:06:27.397 --> 00:06:30.941
We welcome these new
beings of the land.

00:06:32.652 --> 00:06:35.154
- They can call
me Captain Uncle.

00:06:35.155 --> 00:06:38.574
- Uh, I'll go dispose
of this medical waste.

00:06:38.575 --> 00:06:40.869
With a little butter and lemon.

00:06:41.494 --> 00:06:43.704
- Want a picture with the kids?
- No need.

00:06:43.705 --> 00:06:45.873
The way they look is
burned into my mind.

00:06:45.874 --> 00:06:48.584
- They're nice, you know?
Just a kinda little...

00:06:48.585 --> 00:06:49.877
- Super gross.

00:06:49.878 --> 00:06:52.463
- But, you're
finally grandparents.

00:06:52.464 --> 00:06:54.257
- That'll be our little secret.

00:07:05.101 --> 00:07:06.978
Oh my.

00:07:09.105 --> 00:07:11.857
- Thanks for bringing the
kids by for my lunch break.

00:07:11.858 --> 00:07:14.151
- They're the sweetest
thing on the menu.

00:07:14.152 --> 00:07:15.072
Not even close!

00:07:16.529 --> 00:07:18.030
- Uh, question.

00:07:18.031 --> 00:07:21.034
These three babies are
totally different sizes.

00:07:21.868 --> 00:07:22.952
Question mark.

00:07:22.953 --> 00:07:25.287
- Oh, well, they
grew at varying rates

00:07:25.288 --> 00:07:27.873
depending on the temperature
of the water they were in.

00:07:27.874 --> 00:07:31.168
Little Newt here was
in a cold, deep area.

00:07:31.169 --> 00:07:33.420
- Mama!
- Wrong again.

00:07:34.547 --> 00:07:37.257
- Mandy is from the
temperate middle depths.

00:07:37.258 --> 00:07:38.842
- He's shrively!

00:07:38.843 --> 00:07:41.220
You haven't
seen the half of it.

00:07:41.221 --> 00:07:43.430
- And Axl is from
the warm shallows,

00:07:43.431 --> 00:07:45.266
just like his old man.

00:07:45.267 --> 00:07:48.143
Do you always
have to talk about me?

00:07:48.144 --> 00:07:50.604
- So why does this one
keep calling me Mama?

00:07:50.605 --> 00:07:52.356
And what's with
the big weird eye?

00:07:52.357 --> 00:07:54.650
- It's not weird.
It looks like yours.

00:07:54.651 --> 00:07:55.985
It's pretty weird.

00:07:55.986 --> 00:07:57.486
- Why would he look like me?

00:07:57.487 --> 00:07:58.946
- Don't you remember?

00:07:58.947 --> 00:08:01.657
Twenty years ago,
you impregnated Kif.

00:08:01.658 --> 00:08:03.993
- Seriously? Oh, my God.

00:08:03.994 --> 00:08:05.786
I must have been super drunk.

00:08:05.787 --> 00:08:09.164
- Leela, you bone brain!
You didn't have sex.

00:08:09.165 --> 00:08:11.166
Bone.

00:08:11.167 --> 00:08:13.585
- Luckily, there's
an educational movie

00:08:13.586 --> 00:08:17.131
that explains how Kif's
species reproduces.

00:08:17.132 --> 00:08:18.882
And it's filthy.

00:08:18.883 --> 00:08:22.052
YowzaVision
Educational Films

00:08:22.053 --> 00:08:25.556
presents Sex Across
The Universe.

00:08:25.557 --> 00:08:28.392
Oh, yeah!
Educate me, baby.

00:08:28.393 --> 00:08:30.645
This week,
the Amphibiosans.

00:08:31.396 --> 00:08:33.939
For every organism
across the universe,

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:37.610
reproduction is a
steamy, erotic process.

00:08:37.611 --> 00:08:40.195
Except the Amphibiosans.

00:08:40.196 --> 00:08:42.406
They just barely touch hands

00:08:42.407 --> 00:08:45.117
while the rest of us
are gettin' it on.

00:08:45.118 --> 00:08:47.244
Yowza.

00:08:47.245 --> 00:08:48.662
Eh, that
was pretty hot.

00:08:48.663 --> 00:08:51.290
- So, you see, Amy
was my smizmar,

00:08:51.291 --> 00:08:54.877
the one whose mere presence
made me receptive to pregnancy.

00:08:54.878 --> 00:08:57.963
- Which makes me their smizmama.

00:08:57.964 --> 00:09:01.258
- But it was Lila who
contributed the DNA

00:09:01.259 --> 00:09:04.303
when she accidentally
touched Kif's hand.

00:09:04.304 --> 00:09:06.180
- Are you sure I wasn't drunk?

00:09:06.181 --> 00:09:08.766
I-I mean, I'm drunk
now.

00:09:08.767 --> 00:09:10.267
- Mwah!

00:09:10.268 --> 00:09:11.936
- Ew! Mom, Dad!

00:09:11.937 --> 00:09:13.771
Leela!

00:09:13.772 --> 00:09:17.609
Will you stay in
our lovers' story?

00:09:18.276 --> 00:09:21.236
If you stay, you
won't be sorry

00:09:21.237 --> 00:09:23.614
'Cause we believe in you

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:28.911
Soon you'll grow,
so take a chance

00:09:28.912 --> 00:09:33.625
With a couple of kooks
hung up on romancing

00:09:34.376 --> 00:09:38.212
Will you stay in
our lovers' story?

00:09:38.213 --> 00:09:41.799
If you stay, you
won't be sorry

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:43.717
'Cause we believe in you

00:09:45.345 --> 00:09:48.764
Soon, you'll grow,
so take a chance

00:09:48.765 --> 00:09:50.891
With a couple of kooks

00:09:50.892 --> 00:09:53.811
Hung up on romancing

00:09:57.565 --> 00:10:00.276
- Let's reinflate
my head and go home.

00:10:00.277 --> 00:10:04.238
- Yeah. Maybe they'll conk out
and we'll get a little us time.

00:10:10.036 --> 00:10:13.123
Those little guys are
the best, but they're a lot.

00:10:14.124 --> 00:10:16.626
- Well, luckily, there's
two of us to split the work.

00:10:17.877 --> 00:10:19.920
Doop, doo-doo-doop,
doop, doop, doop, doop!

00:10:19.921 --> 00:10:22.089
- Captain Brannigan!
At your service, sir.

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:25.467
- With ease, Lieutenant. I have
a bit of news to say at you.

00:10:25.468 --> 00:10:28.429
- Is it about the baby gifts you claim
you sent? Because we still haven't...

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:30.180
- I'm afraid there's
no time to discuss

00:10:30.181 --> 00:10:32.975
the many presents I bought,
some of which are large.

00:10:32.976 --> 00:10:35.311
Soldier, you are ordered
to report for duty.

00:10:36.313 --> 00:10:39.690
- Is it war?
- I hope so, but we're not sure.

00:10:39.691 --> 00:10:42.484
All we know is that DOOP
has lost radio contact

00:10:42.485 --> 00:10:46.113
with a remote outpost in
Ursa Major. Over and under.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:50.784
- I'm sorry you'll have
to handle the kids alone.

00:10:50.785 --> 00:10:52.286
I'm not worried.

00:10:58.835 --> 00:11:00.502
I love you!

00:11:24.319 --> 00:11:26.195
- Roll call!

00:11:26.196 --> 00:11:29.657
"Four eyes."
"One-eye." "Crab man."

00:11:29.658 --> 00:11:32.076
"Can man." "Who cares?"

00:11:32.077 --> 00:11:33.827
Dammit! Where's Amy?

00:11:33.828 --> 00:11:35.829
What do I need, a bigger antler?

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:38.540
Oh, I'm so, so sorry.

00:11:38.541 --> 00:11:40.209
The babysitter didn't show up.

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:42.127
Ah!

00:11:42.128 --> 00:11:45.297
- Finally. Where are you?
- Sorry, toots.

00:11:45.298 --> 00:11:46.966
I must have the address wrong.

00:11:46.967 --> 00:11:49.385
784 West 28th Street?

00:11:49.386 --> 00:11:52.137
Uh-huh. Weird,
th-that's what I got.

00:11:52.138 --> 00:11:53.931
Oh, Earth! Ah!

00:11:53.932 --> 00:11:56.600
Coulda swore you
said Kepler 10B.

00:11:58.103 --> 00:12:01.730
Guess I'll catch the next
generation ship back to Nutley.

00:12:01.731 --> 00:12:03.565
- Oh...

00:12:03.566 --> 00:12:06.694
- Mom, Mom, Mom! Can you
judge our whispering contest?

00:12:06.695 --> 00:12:08.195
Okay. You ready?

00:12:08.196 --> 00:12:11.240
I lose!

00:12:11.241 --> 00:12:12.574
Oh, come on! Oh...

00:12:17.872 --> 00:12:21.292
- Look at me, chugging
mineral water on a weeknight!

00:12:21.293 --> 00:12:23.335
So wild and free!

00:12:25.422 --> 00:12:27.464
I miss them so.

00:12:27.465 --> 00:12:29.383
- I feel you, soldier.

00:12:29.384 --> 00:12:32.344
And not in a handsy
way this time.

00:12:32.345 --> 00:12:33.804
Mm.

00:12:33.805 --> 00:12:35.181
Sticky...

00:12:36.099 --> 00:12:38.225
Bring a bowl of these
candies to my quarters

00:12:38.226 --> 00:12:39.602
when you're done crying.

00:12:42.647 --> 00:12:45.190
- Thanks for offering to
watch the kids, Leela.

00:12:45.191 --> 00:12:48.277
I need a break so
bad. You have no idea.

00:12:48.278 --> 00:12:51.363
- No, it's clear you're
a wreck, and I get it.

00:12:51.364 --> 00:12:53.407
They're a nightmare.

00:12:53.408 --> 00:12:55.951
A-A sweet, adorable nightmare.

00:12:55.952 --> 00:12:57.786
- That's fair. Kids!

00:12:57.787 --> 00:12:59.913
Mommy's gonna go nap-nap.

00:12:59.914 --> 00:13:02.082
Don't be scared of
Leela. She's very...

00:13:02.083 --> 00:13:03.834
Yay! Mommy Leela!

00:13:03.835 --> 00:13:06.170
Cowabunga, dude!

00:13:10.425 --> 00:13:13.218
- The Clump-O-Honeys you
requested, Capt... Oh jeez.

00:13:15.138 --> 00:13:17.973
If there's nothing further, I will...
- Oh no, you willn't.

00:13:17.974 --> 00:13:21.226
These delicious Clumps
aren't for eating. Mm!

00:13:21.227 --> 00:13:22.937
Mm...

00:13:22.938 --> 00:13:25.022
They're for manscaping.

00:13:25.023 --> 00:13:27.608
Manscape me, Kif.
That's an order.

00:13:27.609 --> 00:13:29.861
Owooga!

00:13:30.654 --> 00:13:32.905
- Ooh!
- Whoa! What's that?

00:13:32.906 --> 00:13:34.782
- I never saw one
of those before,

00:13:34.783 --> 00:13:36.700
and I was born,
like, four days ago.

00:13:36.701 --> 00:13:39.745
- It's a ship loader.
Any hyperactive kids here

00:13:39.746 --> 00:13:43.123
up for a nice, exhausting
treadmill race?

00:13:43.124 --> 00:13:46.543
Oh wow! Cool! I mean, cool.

00:13:46.544 --> 00:13:48.545
- God, I hope this works.

00:14:10.235 --> 00:14:13.946
- Approaching the outpost, sir.
Still no response on any frequency.

00:14:13.947 --> 00:14:16.907
- My God. What the hell
happened down there?

00:14:16.908 --> 00:14:19.660
It looks like the whole
planet has psoriasis.

00:14:19.661 --> 00:14:22.204
- You're looking at the
back of my head, sir.

00:14:33.508 --> 00:14:36.511
- Welcome to
Exobiology Station 38.

00:14:38.096 --> 00:14:40.306
- Dammit! I'm outta laser!

00:14:40.307 --> 00:14:43.392
- Um, hello, sir. Is
this outpost secure?

00:14:43.393 --> 00:14:46.312
The DOOP hasn't received any
response from you in months.

00:14:46.313 --> 00:14:48.814
- Oh, yeah. Transmitter
got ripped up by bears.

00:14:50.108 --> 00:14:52.568
That's what we study here.
Bears. I'm a bear biologist.

00:14:52.569 --> 00:14:55.029
- Sounds like a fun
job that pays bad.

00:14:55.030 --> 00:14:58.490
- I used to be a whale
biologist, but I hate whales.

00:14:58.491 --> 00:14:59.908
Hate them.

00:14:59.909 --> 00:15:02.453
- Well, then it's good you
found an animal you like.

00:15:02.454 --> 00:15:03.662
- Nope. Still looking.

00:15:03.663 --> 00:15:07.082
This bear
species is known as tardigrades.

00:15:07.083 --> 00:15:09.585
It's a fancy word for ugly.

00:15:09.586 --> 00:15:12.338
Oh, shut
up, you stupid bear!

00:15:12.339 --> 00:15:13.881
They're also stupid, by the way.

00:15:13.882 --> 00:15:16.051
I discovered that.
Bear biologist.

00:15:24.186 --> 00:15:26.019
I fixed the transmitter.

00:15:27.228 --> 00:15:29.605
Now, may I please head
home to my family?

00:15:29.606 --> 00:15:31.941
- Without delay. But first,

00:15:31.942 --> 00:15:33.400
candy break?

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:40.824
- Are you bat crackers?

00:15:40.825 --> 00:15:43.370
If they smell human food,
they go bat crackers!

00:15:48.833 --> 00:15:52.544
- It seems they recognize
a fellow apex predator.

00:15:52.545 --> 00:15:54.923
Well, four can
play at that game.

00:15:59.761 --> 00:16:02.389
Kif! Help!

00:16:05.976 --> 00:16:08.686
Let's
go! Faster! Faster!

00:16:08.687 --> 00:16:11.522
Go, horseface, go!

00:16:11.523 --> 00:16:13.650
Neigh!

00:16:14.484 --> 00:16:17.278
Now, buy us ice cream!

00:16:21.616 --> 00:16:24.451
Rum raisin tastes just
like caterpillars!

00:16:24.452 --> 00:16:26.704
- We love you, Leela.

00:16:26.705 --> 00:16:29.873
- Aw, hell no! You're
not the mom of them!

00:16:29.874 --> 00:16:33.002
- What?
- Are you done spoiling my kids rotten

00:16:33.003 --> 00:16:34.753
so they'll love you more?

00:16:34.754 --> 00:16:36.922
- I'm just a beaten-down horse.

00:16:36.923 --> 00:16:39.842
- Well, you can trot
back to the barn now!

00:16:39.843 --> 00:16:43.095
Kif's coming home soon,
and you are not their mom!

00:16:43.096 --> 00:16:45.764
- Uh, actually, I sort of am.

00:16:45.765 --> 00:16:47.767
- Go on! Git! Hyah!

00:16:52.689 --> 00:16:55.190
Oh God, they're nuzzling me!

00:16:56.985 --> 00:16:58.902
Hello?

00:16:58.903 --> 00:17:01.530
- Please come home, Kiffy!

00:17:01.531 --> 00:17:04.950
The kids like Leela more
than me, and it really hurts.

00:17:06.328 --> 00:17:09.079
I'm the worst mom ever.

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:11.415
Except for my own mom.

00:17:11.416 --> 00:17:14.627
Stop licking my
velour! It's dry clean only!

00:17:14.628 --> 00:17:17.171
- Amy, darling, the
children love you.

00:17:17.172 --> 00:17:18.756
And I love you.

00:17:18.757 --> 00:17:21.342
And stay away
from my scrotums!

00:17:21.343 --> 00:17:24.470
- You're their mother,
and you always will be.

00:17:24.471 --> 00:17:26.221
Nothing can change that.

00:17:27.307 --> 00:17:29.975
- Amy Wong, a challenge
has been filed

00:17:29.976 --> 00:17:32.353
for the motherhood
of these children.

00:17:32.354 --> 00:17:35.105
No...

00:17:35.106 --> 00:17:37.146
Amy? Amy,
I'm coming home, I swear.

00:17:39.069 --> 00:17:41.320
I have to leave right now, sir!

00:17:41.321 --> 00:17:44.657
No, Kif! The DOOP
never leaves a man behind!

00:17:44.658 --> 00:17:46.075
Not when I'm the man!

00:17:52.207 --> 00:17:55.668
- Alright, bears. Daddy's
coming to tuck you in...

00:17:56.711 --> 00:17:58.379
to your graves.

00:18:01.591 --> 00:18:03.009
- I'll be out here.

00:18:06.805 --> 00:18:08.806
- Nobody's taking my babies!

00:18:08.807 --> 00:18:10.474
They're everything to me!

00:18:10.475 --> 00:18:13.477
- I appreciate your emotional
shouting in my ear hole,

00:18:13.478 --> 00:18:16.856
but I must intervene whenever
parenthood is called into question.

00:18:18.191 --> 00:18:19.483
- Grand Midwife?

00:18:19.484 --> 00:18:21.986
- Oh, drop the
surprised act, Leela.

00:18:21.987 --> 00:18:24.363
How could you do this?
- Do what?

00:18:24.364 --> 00:18:27.199
Suck the jelly out of the
jelly donuts with a straw?

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:30.452
- This jelly hound did not summon
me. The challenge is automatic

00:18:30.453 --> 00:18:33.998
when tests show the
smizmar contributed no DNA.

00:18:33.999 --> 00:18:36.041
The children
inherited genes

00:18:36.042 --> 00:18:37.876
only from Kif and Leela,

00:18:37.877 --> 00:18:40.754
plus trace DNA from
a certain Scruffy.

00:18:40.755 --> 00:18:43.757
Scruffy's stuff gets around.

00:18:45.343 --> 00:18:48.220
- Should the challenge indicate
someone else is the mother,

00:18:48.221 --> 00:18:49.471
then that person...

00:18:49.472 --> 00:18:51.640
eh, or whatever...

00:18:51.641 --> 00:18:53.142
shall raise the children.

00:18:53.143 --> 00:18:54.476
- But... But...

00:18:54.477 --> 00:18:58.480
- You and Kif must be present for
the challenge tomorrow. Good day.

00:18:59.941 --> 00:19:02.444
Yeah, FYI, y-you've got a
little jelly right there.

00:19:09.951 --> 00:19:12.161
- Did somebody call
an exterminator?

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:23.088
- It's been a blast.
- Help me, Kif!

00:19:23.089 --> 00:19:26.050
They found the secret
candy in my girdle!

00:19:33.808 --> 00:19:36.311
I'm a camouflaged
killing machine.

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:41.398
- I'm...

00:19:41.399 --> 00:19:44.360
I'm sorry I got
so jealous, Leela.

00:19:44.361 --> 00:19:47.404
I just kinda lost it.
- It's okay.

00:19:47.405 --> 00:19:50.699
The bond parents feel with
their kids is intense...

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:51.992
so I hear.

00:19:51.993 --> 00:19:54.703
I'm just
proud I helped you become a mom.

00:19:58.124 --> 00:20:00.250
I hope it works out
for you tomorrow.

00:20:00.251 --> 00:20:01.919
- And if it doesn't,

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:05.422
I'm sure you'll
take good care of them.

00:20:09.886 --> 00:20:12.721
- I refuse to die groveling.

00:20:12.722 --> 00:20:14.390
But I'm open to sniveling.

00:20:24.734 --> 00:20:26.151
Naked Kif,

00:20:26.152 --> 00:20:27.569
you saved my life!

00:20:27.570 --> 00:20:29.530
You have my undying loyalty.

00:20:30.782 --> 00:20:32.157
Eat Kif! He's boneless!

00:20:37.414 --> 00:20:39.581
- This one's for Axl, Mandy,

00:20:39.582 --> 00:20:41.208
and little what's-his-name.

00:21:03.982 --> 00:21:07.610
- I am the Grand Midwife
from the other day,

00:21:07.611 --> 00:21:11.030
inquisitor for the
challenge of Amy Wong.

00:21:11.031 --> 00:21:13.449
Amy, where is your smizmale?

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:15.075
- He isn't with me.

00:21:15.076 --> 00:21:18.954
- Oh, the sorrow! Oh, the shame!

00:21:18.955 --> 00:21:20.414
- There he is!

00:21:22.375 --> 00:21:24.669
- Okay, but it doesn't
lessen the shame.

00:21:25.879 --> 00:21:27.755
- Kif!
- Amy!

00:21:27.756 --> 00:21:29.257
Daddy!

00:21:30.467 --> 00:21:32.343
- I don't remember him.

00:21:32.344 --> 00:21:34.470
- So, like, did
you do war stuff?

00:21:34.471 --> 00:21:37.306
- I did what a Daddy had to do.

00:21:43.313 --> 00:21:46.023
- Bear number 23
was also stupid,

00:21:46.024 --> 00:21:49.318
fighting for scraps while
I dined on salmon tartare.

00:21:51.655 --> 00:21:53.657
None for you, losers!

00:21:57.243 --> 00:21:58.619
Oh!

00:22:05.377 --> 00:22:08.587
- The challenge may play
out over days or weeks

00:22:08.588 --> 00:22:11.966
within the brutal confines
of the Inquisidome.

00:22:11.967 --> 00:22:13.718
Some call it a tiki hut.

00:22:14.052 --> 00:22:17.012
- Leela's gonna watch you
guys while we're in there.

00:22:18.139 --> 00:22:20.183
And maybe a little longer.

00:22:20.558 --> 00:22:22.476
But whatever happens,

00:22:22.477 --> 00:22:24.479
you're going to be okay.

00:22:25.897 --> 00:22:27.648
- You are, too.

00:22:38.576 --> 00:22:41.161
- The challenge is a
challenging challenge,

00:22:41.162 --> 00:22:44.164
dating from when our
language had few words.

00:22:44.165 --> 00:22:46.959
It will incorporate a
battery of genetic tests

00:22:46.960 --> 00:22:49.962
and a full neuropsychological
obstacle course,

00:22:49.963 --> 00:22:52.965
but it begins with
a simple question.

00:22:52.966 --> 00:22:54.133
Amy Wong.

00:22:54.134 --> 00:22:57.803
Do you or do you not
love those children?

00:23:01.683 --> 00:23:04.728
- More than I knew I
could love anything.

00:23:05.937 --> 00:23:07.939
- Which is all
that truly matters.

00:23:08.982 --> 00:23:10.816
The challenge is over.

00:23:10.817 --> 00:23:12.401
You are their mother

00:23:12.402 --> 00:23:15.029
and always will be.

00:23:20.702 --> 00:23:22.661
Oops! That wasn't
supposed to happen.

00:23:22.662 --> 00:23:24.496
Cheap, lousy wall.

00:23:24.497 --> 00:23:28.125
Children! You may now come
hug your mother and father.

00:23:28.126 --> 00:23:30.294
For only a small additional fee.

00:23:33.882 --> 00:23:36.592
- You're my favorite mommy.

00:23:40.972 --> 00:23:42.681
- Who wants treacle?

00:23:45.769 --> 00:23:47.478
- Strong stuff, huh?